    bet.ts:

        protected betOnPony(pony: PonyModel): void {
            const race = this.raceModel.value()!;
            const result$ = this.raceService.bet(race.id, pony.id);
        }
    
  
5️⃣ We now need to display a visual indicator in the template, to identify the pony on which the
    bet has been placed. We will thus add a beautiful green border around the pony that has been
    chosen.
    To achieve that, once the bet has been placed, 👉you will fetch the race again from the server,
    and it will contain an additional attribute betPonyId. 👉Add the field betPonyId to RaceModel,
    and make it optional using a ?. 👉To trigger the refresh, you will tell the resource to reload
    after the bet has been placed (in the subscribe of the bet method).
    👉Create a method isPonySelected(pony) returning true if the ID of the pony matches with the
    betPonyId attribute of the race. 👉Then use this method to dynamically add a CSS class selected
    to the div wrapping the pony.
    race-model.ts:

        export interface RaceModel {
            id: number;
            name: string;
            ponies: Array<PonyModel>;
            startInstant: string;
            betPonyId?: number; 👈
        }

    bet.ts:

        protected betOnPony(pony: PonyModel): void {
            const race = this.raceModel.value()!;
            const result$ = this.raceService.bet(race.id, pony.id)
            result$.subscribe({
                next: () => this.raceModel.reload() 👈
            });
        }

    👉 protected isPonySelected(pony: PonyModel): boolean {
