6️⃣ You probably noticed that if you try to place a bet on a race that has already started
    (or is finished), the bet fails. You should display an error message to the user when that
    happens. Add a div with the CSS classes alert alert-danger alert-dismissible and the
    accessibility attribute role="alert" containing the message: "The race is already started or
    finished", and display this div if the bet fails.
    👉Use a signal named betFailed to achieve that. We want the alert to be closable, so it
    should contain a button like the following:

        <button type="button" class="btn-close" aria-label="Close"></button>

    bet.ts:

        protected readonly betFailed = signal(false);

    A click on this button should reset the betFailed signal to false, hence closing the alert.
    bet.html:

        @if (betFailed()) {
            <div class="alert alert-danger alert-dismissible mb-3" role="alert">
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" aria-label="Close"
                👉(click)="betFailed.set(false)"></button>
                The race is already started or finished
            </div>
        }


7️⃣ A user should also be able to change his mind and cancel his bet. Add a method
    cancelBet(raceId: number): Observable<void> in RaceService
    (see https://ponyracer.ninja-squad.com/apidoc#resources-bet-cancel)

    Then call this cancelBet method from betOnPony() if the pony that has been clicked is the
    selected one. To do so, create a variable that contains this.raceService.cancelBet(…​) if
    the pony is the selected one, or this.raceService.bet(…​) if it isn’t. Then subscribe to
    this variable, with the same subscribe method as before, as we also want to refresh the
    race after a cancelled bet, or display the alert if the cancellation failed.
    bet.ts:

        protected betOnPony(pony: PonyModel): void {
            this.betFailed.set(false);
            const race = this.raceModel.value()!;
        👉 const result$ = this.isPonySelected(pony)
            ? this.raceService.cancelBet(race.id)
            : this.raceService.bet(race.id, pony.id);

            result$.subscribe({
                next: () => this.raceModel.reload(),
                error: () => this.betFailed.set(true) 👈
            }); 
        }


